# kq

Answer KotOR resource questions with the `kq_*` MCP tools, or the `kq` CLI when they are not
connected. Query archives in place; never extract BIF/ERF/RIM/MOD files to search them.

- `-i` is `--install`. Case-insensitive grep is `--ignore-case` only.
- Run `which` before `cat` when a ResRef may exist in several places.
- Output is JSON by default. Exit 3 means no match, 4 means no install resolved.
- The `kq-query` and `kq-formats` skills carry flags and per-format output shapes.
